  88  Table Days_Distribution(FlowType,Days,Nu_SteadyDays) "number of steady and
       unsteady saturdays sundays and weekdays in the month"
  89                           case1   case2   case3   case4   case5   case6  ca
      se7   case8   case9   case10   case11   case12
  90  Steady. Sunday            0       1        2       4      4        4      
      4       4       4       4         4         4
  91  Hydropeak. Sunday         4       3        2       0      0        0      
      0       0       0       0         0         0
  92  Steady. Saturday          0       0        0       0      2        4      
      4       4       4       4         4         4
  93  Hydropeak. Saturday       4       4        4       4      2        0      
      0       0       0       0         0         0
  94  Steady. Weekday           0       0        0       0      0        0      
      1       2       7       12        17        22
  95  Hydropeak. Weekday        22      22       22      22     22       22     
      21      20      15      10        5         0     ;
  96   
  97  Table Energy_Price(d,Price,p)"Price of MegaWatt hour during different days
       and within period p ($ per MWh)"
  98                        pLow        pHigh
  99  Sunday.Contract       37.70       37.70
 100  Sunday.Market         42.70       42.70
 101  Saturday.Contract     37.70       50.61
 102  Saturday.Market       42.70       56.61
 103  Weekday.Contract      37.70       63.52
 104  Weekday.Market        42.70       68.52;
 105   
 106   
 107  Table Nobugflow_Rel(tot_vol,Days,p)"Observed releases of different monthly
       volume on daytypes d and period p  (cfs)"
 108  *V1 The release volume of March 2016 was ~0.72 MAF.
 109  *V2 The release volume of August 2015 was ~0.83 MAF.
 110  *V3 The release volume of August 2017 was ~0.94 MAF.
 111                   pLow        pHigh
 112  V1.Sunday        9171.4       9685.1
 113  V1.Saturday      9559.4      11452.5
 114  V1.Weekday       9702.1      13081.8
 115  V2.Sunday       10535.6      12431.2
 116  V2.Saturday     11461.6      13451.1
 117  V2.Weekday      10983.1      15029.9
 118  V3.Sunday       12820.3      13802.0
 119  V3.Saturday     13039.8      15509.4
 120  V3.Weekday      13115.5      16659.9    ;
 121  *===============================================
 122  SCALAR
 123  Convert                        Conversion factor from cfs to ac-ft per hou
      r (0.0014*60)/0.083/
 124  Daily_RelRange                 Allowable daily release range (cfs)/8000/
 125   
 126  Totaldays                      Total number of days in the month/30/
 127  Nu_Saturdays                   Number of saturdays in the month/4/
 128  Nu_Sun_Holi                    Number of sundays + holidays in the month /
      4/
 129  *Here we are considering an arbitrary monthly calender with exact number o
      f days as in real month but that considered month starts on monday.
 130  *Which means there will be 4 Saturdays and 4 Sundays in the month. We are 
      considering any holidays in the month.
 131  *The real monthly calender can be easily used by changing the number of da
      ys of each day type, if required.
 132  *===============================================
 133  VARIABLES
 134   
 135  ObjectiveVal                    Objective functions value ($)
 136  storage                         Reservoir storage at the end of the month 
      (acre-ft)
 137  Released_vol                    Total water released during the month (ac-
      ft)
 138   
 139  Revenue_zeroSteadyFlow          Revenue genereated from all flowpatterns d
      aytypes and periods when zero number of steady low flow day($)
 140   
 141  Positive Variables
 142   
 143  Revenue(FlowPattern,d,p)        Revenue all ($)
 144   
 145  Release(FlowPattern,d,p)        Reservoir release on different day types a
      nd flow patterns durinng period p (cfs)
 146  Energy_Gen(FlowPattern,d,p)     Hydropower Generated within each timestep 
      during different day types(MWh)
 147   
 148  ;
 149  *===============================================
 150   
 151  EQUATIONS
 152   
 153  *Constraints
 154  EQ1_ResMassBal                                   Reservoir mass balance (a
      cre-ft)
 155  EQ2_reqpowerstorage                              The minimum storage requi
      red for hydropower generation(power pool storage) (acre-ft)
 156  EQ3_maxstor                                      Reservoir Max storage (ac
      re-ft)
 157  EQ4_MaxR(FlowPattern,d,p)                        Max Release for any day t
      ype during any period p but it will not work when NumDays will be zero(cfs
      )
 158  EQ5_MinR(FlowPattern,d,p)                        Min Release for any day t
      ype with flows during any period p but it will not work when NumDays will 
      be zero (cfs)
 159  EQ6_ZeroFlowDays(FlowPattern,d,p)                No release for any day ty
      pe during any period p when Num_Days equal to zero(cfs)
 160  EQ7_Rel_Range(FlowPattern,d)                     Constraining the daily re
      lease range but it will not work when NumDays will be zero(cfs per day)
 161  EQ8_AlternativeDays_Relrange                     Constraining release chan
      ge between on-peak of current day and off-peak of next day to be less than
       or equal to 8000 (cfs)
 162  EQ9_AlternativeDays_Relrange                     Constraining release chan
      ge between on-peak of current day and off-peak of next day to be less than
       or equal to 8000 (cfs)
 163  EQ10_AlternativeDays_Relrange                    Constraining release chan
      ge between on-peak of current day and off-peak of next day to be less than
       or equal to 8000 (cfs)
 164   
 165  EQ11_Monthtlyrel                                 Constraining total monthl
      y release volume (ac-ft)
 166  EQ12_RelVolume                                   Total volume from differe
      nt types of day in the month (ac-ft)
 167   
 168  EQ13_SteadyFlow_Day(d)                           Constraining on-peak and 
      off-peak releases during Steadyflow day to be equal (cfs)
 169  EQ14_OffsetRel                                   Offset release between of
      f-peak unsteady weekday and off-peak steady weekend (saturday or and sunda
      y)releses(cfs)
 170   
 171  EQ15_OnPeak_Saturday                             On-peak Saturday constrai
      nt. i.e. Weekend on-peak minus 2000 cfs (found this value from observed hy
      drographs of 2015 2016 2017).
 172  EQ15a_offpeak_Saturday                           Off-peak Saturday constra
      int (cfs)
 173   
 174  EQ16_OnPeak_Sunday                               On-peak Sunday constraint
      . i.e.  equal to Saturday On-peak.
 175  EQ16a_offpeak_Sunday                             Off-peak Sunday constrain
      t (cfs)
 176   
 177   
 178  EQ17_Steady_Saturdays(p)                         Constraining the steady S
      aturday flows equal to steady sundays flows (cfs)
 179   
 180  ** here I am assuming that steady weekday equals to steady sundays.
 181  EQ18_Steady_Weekdays(p)                          Constraining the steady w
      eekdays flows equal to steady sundays flows (cfs)
 182   
 183  EQ19_OnPeak_UnsteadyDay(d)                       Constraining on-peak unst
      eady day release to be greater than off-peak unsteady release on the same 
      day (cfs)
 184   
 185  EQ20_EnergyGen_Max(FlowPattern,d,p)              Maximum Energy Generation
       Limit of the Glen Caynon Dam(MW)
 186  EQ21_EnergyGen(FlowPattern,d,p)                  Energy generated in each 
      period p during different day types (MWh)
 187   
 188  *Objective Functions
 189   
 190  EQ22_Unsteady_days                              Revenue generated during u
      nsteady Days ($).  For all scenarios except hydropeaking hydrograph--Zero 
      Steady low flow days($)
 191   
 192  EQ23_Unbounded(d,p)                              To tackle Unbounded ray e
      rror in case of flat hydrograph
 193  EQ24_Steadydays_Onpeak                          Revenue generated during o
      n-peak Steadyday ($).
 194  EQ25_Steadydays_Offpeak                         Revenue generated during o
      ff-peak Steadyday ($)
 195  EQ26_TotalRevenue                               Total monthly Hydropower R
      evenue generated($). The revenue has all daytypes and all flowpatterns wit
      h both market and contract prices.
 196  ;
 197   
 198   
 199   
 200  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 201   
 202  *Mass Balance Equation
 203  EQ1_ResMassBal..                               storage =e= Initstorage + (
      Inflow*Convert*sum(p,Duration(p))*Totaldays)- Released_vol - evap;
 204  *                                                                         
       CFS * conversion factor from cfs to ac-ft/hr and multiplied by 24 (total 
      duration in a day) then multiplied by total day in the month
 205  *=======================Physical Constraints==============================
      =======
 206  EQ2_reqpowerstorage..                          storage =g= minstorage;
 207  EQ3_maxstor..                                  storage =l= maxstorage;
 208   
 209  EQ4_MaxR(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) gt 0)..                
           Release(FlowPattern,d,p)=l= maxRel;
 210   
 211  EQ5_MinR(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) gt 0)..                
           Release(FlowPattern,d,p)=g= minRel;
 212   
 213  EQ6_ZeroFlowDays(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) eq 0)..        
           Release(FlowPattern,d,p)=e=0;
 214   
 215  EQ7_Rel_Range(FlowPattern,d)$(Num_Days(FlowPattern,d) gt 0)..             
           Release(FlowPattern,d,"pHigh")- Release(FlowPattern,d,"pLow")=l=Daily
      _RelRange;
 216   
 217  EQ8_AlternativeDays_Relrange$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Sunday") gt 0)..      
           Release("HydroPeak","Saturday","pHigh")- Release("HydroPeak","Sunday"
      ,"pLow")=l=Daily_RelRange;
 218  EQ9_AlternativeDays_Relrange$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Saturday") gt 0) ..   
           Release("HydroPeak","Weekday","pHigh")- Release("HydroPeak","Saturday
      ","pLow")=l=Daily_RelRange;
 219  EQ10_AlternativeDays_Relrange..                                           
           Release("HydroPeak","Sunday","pHigh")- Release("HydroPeak","Weekday",
      "pLow")=l=Daily_RelRange;
 220   
 221   
 222  *EQ11_  constraining the overall monthly released volume..
 223  EQ11_Monthtlyrel..                                                        
            TotMonth_volume=e= Released_vol;
 224   
 225  EQ12_RelVolume..                                                          
            Released_vol=e= sum(FlowPattern,sum(d, sum(p, Release(FlowPattern,d,
      p)*Convert*Duration(p))*Num_Days(FlowPattern,d)));
 226   
 227  *======================Managerial Constraints=============================
      ======================
 228   
 229  EQ13_SteadyFlow_Day(d)$(Num_days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0)..               
                   Release("Steady",d,"pHigh") =e= Release("Steady",d,"pLow");
 230   
 231  * EQ14_  finds the minimimum release value from the hydrograph plus additi
      onal release we desire on weekends above off-peak weekday release (i.e. Of
      fset).
 232   
 233  EQ14_OffsetRel$((Num_days("HydroPeak","Weekday") gt 0) and (Num_Days("Stea
      dy","Sunday") gt 0))..                                       Release("Stea
      dy","Sunday","pLow")=e= Release("HydroPeak","Weekday","pLow")+ Weekend_Rel
      ;
 234   
 235  EQ15_OnPeak_Saturday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Saturday") gt 0)..            
                         Release("HydroPeak","Saturday","pHigh")=e= Release("Hyd
      roPeak","Weekday","pHigh")-2000;
 236   
 237  EQ15a_offpeak_Saturday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Saturday") gt 0)..          
                         Release("HydroPeak","Saturday","pLow")=e=  Release("Hyd
      roPeak","Weekday","pLow");
 238   
 239   
 240  EQ16_OnPeak_Sunday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Sunday") gt 0)..                
             Release("HydroPeak","Sunday","pHigh")=e= Release("HydroPeak","Weekd
      ay","pHigh")-2000;
 241  EQ16a_offpeak_Sunday$(Num_days("HydroPeak","Sunday") gt 0)..              
             Release("HydroPeak","Sunday","pLow")=e= Release("HydroPeak","Weekda
      y","pLow");
 242   
 243   
 244  EQ17_Steady_Saturdays(p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Saturday")gt 0)..   Release("
      Steady","Saturday",p)=e= Release("Steady","Sunday",p);
 245  ** Eq 18 assumes that steady weekday equals the steady sunday releases.
 246  EQ18_Steady_Weekdays(p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Weekday")gt 0)..     Release("
      Steady","Weekday",p)=e= Release("Steady","Sunday",p);
 247   
 248   
 249  EQ19_OnPeak_UnsteadyDay(d)$(Num_Days("HydroPeak",d)gt 0)..                
          Release("HydroPeak",d,"pHigh")=g= Release("HydroPeak",d,"pLow");
 250   
 251  EQ20_EnergyGen_Max(FlowPattern,d,p)..                                     
           Energy_Gen(FlowPattern,d,p)=l= 1320*Duration(p);
 252  *Maximum Energy Generation capacity of GCD (MWH).. Source https://www.usbr
      .gov/uc/rm/crsp/gc
 253  EQ21_EnergyGen(FlowPattern,d,p)..                                         
           Energy_Gen(FlowPattern,d,p)=e= Release(FlowPattern,d,p)*Duration(p)*0
      .03715;
 254  * Energy generation formula used in WAPA Execl model..
 255   
 256  *==============================Objective Function=========================
      =============
 257  EQ22_Unsteady_days(FlowPattern,d,p)$((Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0)and
      (Num_Days("Hydropeak","Weekday") gt 0))..          Revenue("HydroPeak",d,p
      )=e= [{ Observed_Rel(d,p)* Energy_Price(d,"Contract",p)+ (Release("HydroPe
      ak",d,p)- Observed_Rel(d,p))*Energy_Price(d,"Market",p)}*0.03715*Duration(
      p)]* Num_Days("HydroPeak",d);
 258   
 259  EQ23_Unbounded(d,p)$(Num_Days("Hydropeak","Weekday") eq 0)..              
                                                           Revenue("HydroPeak",d
      ,p)=e=0;
 260   
 261  EQ24_Steadydays_Onpeak(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0)
      ..                        Revenue("Steady",d,"pHigh")=e=  [{ Release("Stea
      dy",d,"pHigh")* Energy_Price(d,"Contract","pHigh")-(Observed_Rel(d,"pHigh"
      )-Release("Steady",d,"pHigh"))*Energy_Price(d,"Market","pHigh")}*Duration(
      "pHigh")*0.03715]* Num_Days("Steady",d);
 262  EQ25_Steadydays_Offpeak(FlowPattern,d,p)$(Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") gt 0
      )..                       Revenue("Steady",d,"pLow")=e=  [{Observed_Rel(d,
      "pLow")* Energy_Price(d,"Contract","pLow") + (Release("Steady",d,"pLow")- 
      Observed_Rel(d,"pLow"))*Energy_Price(d,"Market","pLow")}*Duration("pLow")*
      0.03715]* Num_Days("Steady",d);
 263   
 264  EQ26_TotalRevenue..                                                       
                               ObjectiveVal=e= Sum((FlowPattern,d,p),Revenue(Flo
      wPattern,d,p));
 265   
 266  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 267   
 268  MODEL Model1 Find value of hydropower revenue using LP/ALL/;
 269  *This model is for all cases of steady flow days. But the results of zero 
      steady low flow days scenario are incorrect so we need seperate model for 
      that.
 270   
 271  Loop((Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays),
 272   
 273  Weekend_Rel= Diff_Release(Offset);
 274  TotMonth_volume = Vol_monthlyrelease(tot_vol);
 275  Observed_Rel(Days,p)= Nobugflow_Rel(tot_vol,Days,p);
 276  Num_Days(FlowType,Days)= Days_Distribution(FlowType,Days,Nu_SteadyDays)+ E
      PS;
 277   
 278  option LP= CPLEX;
 279   
 280  Solve Model1 using LP MAXIMIZE ObjectiveVal;
 281   
 282  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      ---------------------------------------------
 283  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      ---------------------------------------------
 284  * All the following lines of code are saving values for different paramete
      rs
 285   
 286    FStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays)= ObjectiveVal.L;
 287   
 288  * XStore store the energy generated (Mwh/day) during different types of da
      ys
 289     XStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days)= sum (p,Energy_Gen.L
      (FlowType,Days,p))+ EPS;
 290   
 291  * RStore store the reservoir releases (cfs) during different types of days
       and scenarios.
 292     RStore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days,p)= Release.L(FlowTyp
      e,Days,p)+ EPS;
 293   
 294  *Sstore store the end of month reservoir storage (ac-ft)
 295     Sstore(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays)= storage.L + EPS;
 296   
 297  Rev(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,FlowType,Days,p)=  Revenue.L(FlowType,Day
      s,p) +EPS;
 298   
 299  *Saving the model status for different scenarios.
 300     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,"SolStat")= Model1.solvestat;
 301     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,Nu_SteadyDays,"ModStat")= Model1.modelstat;
 302   
 303    option clear=ObjectiveVal,clear=Release,clear=Energy_Gen;
 304  );
 305   
 306   
 307  *+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
      ++++++++++++
 308  * Model for Zero steady Low flow day scenario.
 309   
 310  Equation
 311  EQ27_ZeroBugDays_Revenue                         Revenue generated from al
      l flowpatterns daytypes and periods with zero steady low flow days($)
 312  ;
 313   
 314  EQ27_ZeroBugDays_Revenue$(Num_Days("Steady","Sunday") eq 0)..            R
      evenue_zeroSteadyFlow =e= sum(FlowPattern,sum(d, sum(p,Energy_Gen(FlowPatt
      ern,d,p)*Energy_Price(d,"Contract",p))*Num_Days(FlowPattern,d)));
 315   
 316   
 317  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
 318   
 319  MODEL Model0 Find value of hydropower revenue at zero steady flow days usi
      ng LP/ALL/;
 320  *This model is for zero steady low flow days only
 321   
 322   
 323  Num_Days(FlowType,Days)= Days_Distribution(FlowType,Days,"Case1")+ EPS;
 324   
 325  Loop((Offset,tot_vol),
 326   
 327  Weekend_Rel= Diff_Release(Offset);
 328  TotMonth_volume = Vol_monthlyrelease(tot_vol);
 329   
 330   
 331  option LP= CPLEX;
 332   
 333  Solve Model0 using LP MAXIMIZE Revenue_zeroSteadyFlow;
 334   
 335   
 336  * All the following lines of code are saving values for different paramete
      rs
 337    FStore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1")=Revenue_zeroSteadyFlow.L;
 338   
 339  * XStore store the energy generated (Mwh/day) during different types of da
      ys
 340     XStore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1",FlowType,Days)= sum (p,Energy_Gen.L(FlowT
      ype,Days,p))+ EPS;
 341   
 342  * RStore store the reservoir releases (cfs) during different types of days
       and scenarios.
 343     RStore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1",FlowType,Days,p)= Release.L(FlowType,Days
      ,p)+ EPS;
 344   
 345  *Sstore store the end of month reservoir storage (ac-ft)
 346     Sstore(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1")= storage.L;
 347   
 348   
 349  *Saving the model status for different scenarios.
 350     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1","SolStat")= Model0.solvestat;
 351     ModelResults(Offset,tot_vol,"Case1","ModStat")= Model0.modelstat;
 352  );
 353   
 354   
 355  DISPLAY FStore,XStore,RStore,Sstore;
 356   
 357  *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
      -----*
